# Grammar calls a noun made from a verb a nominalization (`decision`
# from `decide`). Most phrases here are a weak verb plus a noun that
# names the real verb (`make a decision`, `perform a lookup`, `take into
# account`). Others pair a form of `be` with an adjective or a phrase
# that does the same (`is dependent on`, `is in violation of`). The list
# names each phrase in full. A pattern such as
# `[make, perform] DET NOUN` also matches `make a copy` and
# `perform the request`, where the noun is the object and no single
# verb replaces the pair.
#
# Each verb carries its forms for tense and person. `$perform` expands
# to perform, performs, performed, and performing through Harper's
# dictionary, and the lists below add what the dictionary leaves out,
# such as `made`, `took`, and `drew`. `provide` lists its forms by hand,
# because `$provide` also matches `provider` (`provider support for
# Kubernetes`).
#
# `make a request` stays out, because the bare verb reads worse in most
# hits (`to make a request with custom headers`). `gain access to`
# counts, though in the security sense (`an attacker exploits a flaw to
# gain access`) the verb `access` loses the sense of obtaining.
#
# It hit 97 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 20 of 20 sampled hits
# had one verb that replaces the pair.
expr make [$make, made]
expr take [$take, taking, took, taken]
expr give [$give, gave, given]
expr provide [provide, provides, provided, providing]
expr have [has, have, had, having]
expr be [is, are, was, were]
expr main [(@make [(a decision), (the decision), decisions, (a choice), (a comparison), (an assumption), (the assumption), (an attempt), (use of), (a determination), (a distinction), (a selection), (a call to), (changes to), (a change to), modifications, (a modification to)]), ($perform [(a check), validation, (a lookup), (an update), (an analysis), (a search), (a comparison)]), (@take [(a look), action, (into consideration), (into account)]), (@give [consideration, (an indication), (a description of)]), (@provide [(support for), (a description of)]), (@be in charge of), (@be in violation of), ([$gain, $obtain] access to), ($conduct [(a review), (an analysis)]), ([do, does, did, doing] a comparison), (@have [(an effect on), (an impact on), (a need for)]), ($reach [(a decision), (the conclusion)]), ([$come, came] to [a, the] conclusion), ([$draw, drew, drawn] a conclusion), (@be [(indicative of), (reflective of), (dependent on), (dependent upon), (reliant on)]), (in need of), ([$put, putting] emphasis on), ($place emphasis on), (@be of [importance, significance, use])]
let message "Nominalization. Use the verb."
let description "Flags a weak verb plus noun where one verb does the work."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The decoder makes a copy of the buffer before it writes."
allows "The client performs the request and returns the body."
allows "Set decides which bucket receives the token."
allows "Provider support for Kubernetes varies by cloud."
